course: dictionary
lesson: 12972
title: Breathing out: exhalation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exhalation is a noun. It is the word for breathing out, which means pushing air out of your lungs. The verb is exhale. Breathing has two parts: inhalation (breathing in) and exhalation (breathing out).
explain: «Take a slow exhalation and let your shoulders drop.» The clues are slow and let your shoulders drop. Those tell you the word is about breathing out, and that it helps you relax. Swap in "breathing out" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Exhalation can also mean the air, steam or smell that is breathed out or given off. «On a frosty morning, each exhalation made a little white cloud.» The clues are frosty and white cloud. You can see the breath in the cold air, so the word means the air you breathe out.
fact: Exhalation means breathing out: pushing air out of your lungs.
fact: Exhalation can also mean the air, steam or smell that is breathed out or given off.
fact: Inhalation is breathing in, and exhalation is breathing out.
fact: During exhalation, the diaphragm relaxes and the chest gets smaller.
fact: A slow exhalation can help you relax, so calm lessons often use it.
exercise: «On a frosty morning, each exhalation made a little white cloud.» What is an exhalation here? | A loud shout from the chimney | A cold drink on a winter day | *Breath or steam breathed out
exercise: In a calm lesson, the teacher says, «Take a slow exhalation.» What should you do? | Shout the word out loud | *Breathe out slowly | Breathe in as fast as you can | Hold your breath for a minute
exercise: Inhalation and exhalation are opposites. Which word means breathing out? | Diaphragm | Inhalation | *Exhalation | Lungs
test: «The singer took a deep breath, then let out a slow exhalation before she began.» What does exhalation mean here? | *Breathing out slowly | Coughing loudly | Singing a long note | Breathing in deeply
test: During exhalation, what happens to the chest? | It gets bigger | It fills with water | *It gets smaller | It stays exactly the same size
exam: Which best explains exhalation? | Sneezing into a tissue | Holding your breath under water | Breathing in through the nose | *Breathing out, pushing air out of the lungs
